WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
We are now moving into the next section, bleeding and wounds.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.320
Before you ever touch a wound, whether it's minor like a small scrape,

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.560
or major and life-threatening, remember to scan your surroundings for danger

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.080
and make sure you have your gloves and other PPE on.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.240
As we walk through these next few slides, I want you to keep one word fixed in

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.840
your mind, pressure. That is going to be your most

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:28.480
powerful tool for stopping blood loss. To help you get a feel for how this works

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.520
in a real situation, your instructor may pass out some

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.520
materials to everyone now. Each of you should have a pair of gloves,

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.560
two squares of gauze, and one roll of gauze.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.240
Go ahead and get those ready at your stations. We'll be using them in the

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.439
upcoming slides.

